+	  binfmt_flat binary, anonymous malloc, brk-grown heap) is satisfied
+	  by ONE physically contiguous page range from the buddy allocator.
+	  Small NOMMU machines fragment the buddy heap quickly, leaving
+	  several megabytes of free memory but no free blocks of the order
+	  needed to fork a non-trivial process or to malloc more than a few
+	  hundred kilobytes. CONFIG_CMA — the usual answer — depends on MMU.
+
+	  Saying Y here lets a platform device tree describe a reserved
+	  memory region (compatible "linux,nommu-userspace-pool") that the
+	  NOMMU mmap path will draw large user allocations from before
+	  falling back to the buddy allocator.
+
+	  When this option is enabled but no DT node is present, the hook
+	  is a no-op and the buddy fallback is used unconditionally.
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
